5. MODIFIED DISTRIBUTIONS

A "Modified Distribution" is any publicly distributed version of a
Covered Project that incorporates Original Project Work and contains
changes that have not been published or expressly accepted as part of
an official release of the applicable Covered Project.

A Modified Distribution may be used, modified, redistributed, or sold,
but it must comply with all of the following conditions.

5.1 DIFFERENT PROJECT NAME

A Modified Distribution must use a project name clearly distinct from:

    AirPort_RTW88

and:

    Realtek88LegacyAirport

as applicable.

The name of a Covered Project must not be used as the primary name of
a modified project, repository, package, product, driver, distribution,
or release.

5.2 NO FALSE OFFICIAL CONTINUATION

A Modified Distribution must not be represented as:

- an official release of a Covered Project;
- an official continuation of a Covered Project;
- an official successor to a Covered Project;
- a new official version of a Covered Project;
- or the official repository or distribution source for a Covered
  Project.

5.3 VERSION NUMBERS AND PRESENTATION

A Modified Distribution must not use version numbering, repository
presentation, release naming, package metadata, or branding in a manner
that reasonably presents it as an official release or continuation of
a Covered Project.

For example, a modified fork of AirPort_RTW88 must not simply continue
the official AirPort_RTW88 release sequence while presenting itself as
AirPort_RTW88.

The same requirement applies to Realtek88LegacyAirport.

5.4 ATTRIBUTION IS ALLOWED

Truthful attribution is permitted and encouraged.

A Modified Distribution may use statements such as:

    "Based on AirPort_RTW88"

    "Fork of AirPort_RTW88"

    "Derived from AirPort_RTW88"

    "Based on Realtek88LegacyAirport"

    "Fork of Realtek88LegacyAirport"

or equivalent wording that accurately describes the origin of the work.

Such attribution does not permit the modified project itself to use the
Covered Project's name as its own primary identity.

5.5 RENAMING ALONE DOES NOT REMOVE THESE OBLIGATIONS

Changing only the project name, repository name, package metadata,
version number, copyright notice, or branding does not cause Original
Project Work to cease being governed by this License.

The permissions and obligations of this License remain applicable to
Original Project Work contained in the Modified Distribution.

6. UNMODIFIED REDISTRIBUTION

A verbatim and unmodified copy of an official Covered Project release
may retain its original project name.

Such redistribution is permitted provided that:

(a) it is clearly identified as an unmodified copy;

(b) this License and all applicable notices are preserved;

(c) the distributor does not claim authorship of work they did not
    create;

(d) the distributor does not claim to be the official maintainer; and

(e) the distributor does not falsely represent their repository or
    distribution channel as the official source of the Covered Project.

